---
fmContentType: glossaryEntry
term: "CBN (Cannabinol)"
letter: "C"
anchor: "cbn"
category: "cannabinoids"
---

A minor cannabinoid formed when THC degrades over time through exposure to heat, light, or oxygen. Aged or improperly stored cannabis contains higher CBN concentrations. CBN is mildly psychoactive — much less so than THC — and is commonly associated with sedation, though the evidence for this specific effect is limited. Often marketed in sleep products.
